+# Field notes — packet-plumber-v2-estate-spawning (2026-08-22)
+
+- **The bmad-build render pipeline HALTs on multi-module bmad installs** (packet-plumber has bmm+gds; `{{.implementation_artifacts}}` resolves ambiguously). Workaround used: temporarily drop the gds duplicate keys from `_bmad/config.toml`, render, restore byte-equal (both modules point at identical paths, so the render is faithful). Worth flagging upstream — no prior repo has ever rendered bmad-build successfully.
+- **5.12's soft-bias estates were 37% stray under the strict lens** — two real defects the strict audit exposed: the compass draw's diagonals place attach candidates at dist×√2 (outside radius 5, inside any seed floor) and the derived cluster view's dead-slot id=0 collides with cluster 0's id (raw id match could anchor an "attach" on a ROUTER). The mechanism-exact audit (rebuild the derived view over the then-live subset per spawn; ATTACH iff an eligible cluster has a member within radius) is the durable pin shape — it catches both classes and pins cap adherence.
+- **Patch rounds that touch only tests/comments/validation at valid defaults shift ZERO goldens** — verify with a full `harness run` before assuming a re-bless; the deliberate re-bless (fold-check PASS, splice-proofed) is only needed when catalog bytes or the rng interleaving actually move.
