+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** Health / pool / SLA gauges snap value-to-value; when values move fast (drain, refill, SLA decay) the player reads a strobe, not a level (viscomm audit finding B).
+
+**Approach:** Each gauge carries a render-owned display value that eases toward the raw sim value via a pinned 16-entry stepped table (EASE16, the PULSE16 §10.4 pattern), driven purely by game tick. Sim semantics untouched (render-side only); a table-driven one-shot chunk-flash cues large instantaneous jumps, then the ease runs.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Eased display reads ONLY through `gauge_read` (single source — draws never re-derive); raw truth channels (numbers, counters, breach latches, colors) stay raw.
+- Golden-safe BY CONSTRUCTION: the harness capture path never feeds gauge targets, so an unfed gauge reads raw exactly — every T2 golden byte-identical, zero re-bless (the pkt_interp precedent).
+- Deterministic + tick-driven: display is a pure function of (gauge state, tick); identical ticks render identical frames.
+- Reduced-motion (7.3/E9.2, `View.reduced_motion`) snaps display to raw immediately and suppresses the chunk-flash.
+- No transcendentals in draw paths — table lookups + multiplies only (compile-time `when` guards pin table endpoints/shape).
+- First reading after reset seeds display = raw (no 0→value fill animation at run start).
+
+**Ask First:** Any golden image shifts (STOP + flag — canon decision); any change to SLA/health/pool SEMANTICS or serialization.
+
+**Never:** No core/ changes (ODN-1: view reads snapshots only); no wall-clock sampling; no easing of delivered/dropped counters (counters are monotone truth, not levels); no per-frame heap churn.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Unfed gauge (harness) | zero-value Gauges, any tick | `gauge_read` returns raw exactly | N/A (byte-identical goldens) |
+| Target moves (app) | raw 100→60 at tick T | display: 100 at T (no pop), monotone approach, == 60 at arrival, stays | N/A |
+| Target moves continuously | small deltas each tick | same tween chases the moving target; display continuous (no jump at retarget) | N/A |
+| Chunk jump | instantaneous delta ≥ CHUNK_PCT | flash cue fires ONCE at that tick, table-fades over CHUNK_FLASH ticks; tween re-anchors from current display; then eases | N/A |
+| Refill jump | large delta upward | same cue + ease (ghost region = gained chunk) | N/A |
+| Reduced motion | `reduced_motion` = true | display = raw immediately; target feed no-ops; flash suppressed | N/A |
+| Fresh run | `gauge_reset` then first feed | display seeds = raw, zero animation | N/A |
+| Paused | no tick advance | phase frozen (derived from tick) — ease freezes with the sim | N/A |
+| SLA class roster > 8 | class index ≥ 8 | gauge unfed → raw fallback (no tween) | defensive skip |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
