+# Brief — Camera Zoom Tiers + Node-vs-Puck Legibility Rebalance
+
+**Repo:** `/Users/moses/code/packet-plumber` (Odin + raylib), branch `v2`.
+**Governing doc:** `project-context.md` (read it first; it carries the golden
+discipline + the Odin/raylib rules). Follow the repo's existing PR/story flow.
+**Start by creating a feature branch** off `v2` (name it e.g.
+`packet-plumber-v2-camera-zoom-tiers`).
+
+## User directive (verbatim intent)
+
+> "after the last update with zoom and map in PP, now even zoomed in I can
+> barely see the buildings, and the routers are big — the scale is all messed
+> up. Default should be zoomed in, to see the buildings and the links, then an
+> extra zoom in for the node/link click, then zoom out is just to see all the
+> links and the job done across the map — showing the backbone connected
+> between different clusters of buildings across the map."
+
+Confirmed design decisions (user-selected):
+- **Default zoom = ~2.0x** (cluster area — buildings + links legible on entry).
+- **The "buildings" to fix are the terminal node blocks** (the game nodes:
+  Content_Host / Small_Biz / Campus / houses) — NOT the low-poly map underlay
+  texture. Do not rework the Blender underlay; leave it.
+- **Cap/soften the router pucks** so they stop dominating the terminal blocks.
+- **Auto-pullback settles back to the 2.0x default**, not the whole-map fit.
+
+## Current state (what you're changing)
+
+- Camera state lives in `App` (`app/main.odin` ~L236-252): `cam_zoom`,
+  `cam_zoom_to`, `cam_wx/wx_to`, `cam_wy/wy_to`, `pullback`.
+- `camera_set_fit(app)` sets `cam_zoom_to = 1.0` + center = world center. It is
+  currently used for: boot, run reset, AND the selection-deselect home
+  (`camera_set_selection`'s else branch, ~L1762).
+- `camera_set_selection(app)`: node select -> 2.3, link select -> 2.6, else ->
+  `camera_set_fit`.
+- `render/camera.odin`: `CAM_ZOOM_MIN = 1.0` (whole-map bird's-eye),
+  `CAM_ZOOM_MAX = 4.0`, `CAM_ZOOM_STEP = 1.25`; `camera_pullback_target`
+  clamps its lower bound to `CAM_ZOOM_MIN` (the "fit-view floor if beyond").
+- Terminal block size (`render/dublin.odin`): `DUBLIN_NODE_BLOCK_L = 0.40`,
+  `DUBLIN_NODE_BLOCK_W = 0.22` (world tiles).
+- Router puck size (`render/sprites.odin`): `sprite_puck_target` =
+  `1.15 * tile_px * scale * (bbox[ idx ] / base)`, base=110. High-tier pucks
+  (bbox>110) grow above that; `draw_router` (`render/view.odin`) blits via it.
+- `camera_update` (`app/main.odin` ~L1792) sets `v.scale = fit * cam_zoom` and
+  `v.lane_detail = cam_zoom > 1.5`.
+
+## Changes to make
+
+### A. Three-tier zoom model (`app/main.odin` + `app/render/camera.odin`)
+
+1. Add `DEFAULT_ZOOM :: 2.0` to `app/render/camera.odin` (next to the
+   `CAM_ZOOM_*` constants) with a comment: the cluster/default zoom, the
+   resting home; the whole-map bird's-eye is only the manual zoom-out floor.
+2. Add `camera_set_default(app)`: center on the **source terminal / first
+   cluster** (see center note below) with `cam_zoom_to = DEFAULT_ZOOM`,
+   `pullback = false`. Keep it as its own proc; do not overload
+   `camera_set_fit`.
+3. The three tiers must be explicit and non-overlapping:
+   - **Default (entry / run start / deselect home):** `camera_set_default` ->
+     `DEFAULT_ZOOM` (2.0).
+   - **Focus (node/link click):** existing `camera_set_selection` at 2.3 /
+     2.6 — unchanged.
+   - **Out (whole-map backbone / job-done):** manual wheel-out floor
+     `CAM_ZOOM_MIN = 1.0` — unchanged.
+4. Replace the *resting* `camera_set_fit(app)` calls (boot, run reset, and the
+   selection-deselect else-branch at ~L1762) with `camera_set_default(app)`.
+   The whole-map `camera_set_fit` remains only as the explicit out-limit /
+   not-the-resting-home. Do NOT change what the wheel-out floor produces.
+5. **Pullback floor:** change `camera_pullback_target` so its lower clamp is
+   `DEFAULT_ZOOM` (2.0) instead of `CAM_ZOOM_MIN` — the pullback eases out
+   **just enough to include the new district**, then settles back at the 2.0x
+   default. Tradeoff to DOCUMENT in the PR: a district seeded beyond the 2.0
+   viewport may sit at the edge rather than forcing a full-out bird's-eye;
+   that is the accepted behavior (the player stays in the zoomed-in mindset).
+   Update the camera_test pins that asserted the 1.0 fit floor.
+
+### B. Terminal blocks legible (`app/render/dublin.odin`)
+
+Increase `DUBLIN_NODE_BLOCK_L` (0.40 -> ~0.55) and `DUBLIN_NODE_BLOCK_W`
+(0.22 -> ~0.30) so the street-aligned terminal blocks read clearly at the 2.0x
+default — they currently render ~3x smaller than the pucks. Keep the blocks
+street-aligned and non-overlapping with roads/streets (validate the sizing
+against the street layout; if a block overruns its street, reduce toward the
+middle of the range).
+
+### C. Cap/soften router pucks (`app/render/sprites.odin` + `app/render/view.odin`)
+
+In `sprite_puck_target`, clamp the high-tier growth factor (`bbox[idx]/base`)
+to a max (e.g. ~1.30) and trim the base multiplier (1.15 -> ~1.05) so a
